  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Niassa Integrated HIV and AIDS Programme - Caritas Lichinga</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will establish and strengthen comprehensive home-based care and food security for vulnerable households with an emphasis on agricultural techniques suitable for households affected by HIV and an effective prevention programme targeted at young people and other vulnerable people in the community.  It will also strengthen links to national level networks that are campaigning on quality care and treatment.  This is an innovative programme that brings about a partnership between more traditional service providers of HIV and livelihoods support, combined with grass root community based organisations, including associations of PLWHA, to ensure the rights of PLWHA are central to the response.
This partners responsability lies mainly with the provision of better livelihoods to PLWHA and their families and those affected by HIV/AIDS in teh communities. The other responsability lies in the area of esnuring that PLWHA and people affected by HIV/aids do have a broader understanding of their rights and strenghten their voice in obtaining those rights.</narrative>
  </description>
